cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "DynTrust-FedIDS++: Optimization-Based Trust Aggregation for Privacy-Aware Byzantine-Robust Federated Intrusion Detection under Data Drift"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2025-09-20"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_USERNAME/DynTrust-FedIDS-plusplus"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "REPLACE"
    given-names: "Author1"
  - family-names: "REPLACE"
    given-names: "Author2"
keywords:
  - Federated Learning
  - Intrusion Detection
  - Byzantine Robustness
  - Trust-Aware Aggregation
  - Differential Privacy
  - Data Drift
  - Optimisation-based Aggregation
  - FISTA
  - Non-IID
  - Class Imbalance
abstract: >
  DynTrust-FedIDS++ is a federated intrusion-detection framework that unifies
  optimisation-based adaptive aggregation (FISTA), multi-criteria client trust
  estimation, Gaussian differential privacy, and drift-aware residual analysis.
  Evaluated on four real flow-level datasets (NF-CSE-CIC-IDS2018, NF-ToN-IoT,
  UNSW-NB15, CIDDS-001) under 30% Byzantine participation with the ALIE attack.
